{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>A Canaanite man.</b> Some say [it means] merchant, as in \"a Canaanite with balances of deceit in his hand\" (Hosea 12:8), and with the addition of a yod, \"and there shall be no Canaanite any more\" (Zechariah 14:21). And it is possible [that it is] according to its plain meaning. And the Sages said that \"Judah went down\" [means] that he went down from his greatness, and this is the way of derash, for one who comes from the northern side of the world to its southern side goes down, and those who pursue investigation will understand that this is true."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:47:21.568425273Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}